 and the easy difficulty then you  would have a lower chance now you can  get loot anywhere but if you'll if you  Laurel out there to be like I want to  become the most powerful person in the  world you'll find that efficiency mark  of like difficulty and challenging  content and you want to do harder stuff  to get those better  rewards because drops are dictated by  pilot level and not gear score this  means that if you decide to swap  javelins it won't take long for you to  trick it out with decent gear once you  hit pilot level 30 you unlock three new  difficulty levels this is when things  get a bit harder and you'll start  getting some very rare loot so at level  30 the three new difficulty is open  that's Grand Master one two and three  and that again will increase the the  loot drop chance so you know it kind of  goes like I said uncommon common rare  epic master work legendary so you get to  a point where you really want those  master works and Legendary's that's  where like the fun properties come in  that change how you play the change of  builds that that like you know a weak  point strike you get it'll reload you  get a free charge you know things like  that that totally change how you play  kind of create builds and rotations and  stuff like that so when you really want  lots of them that's when you'll start  pushing Grand Master one two and three  and you'll need to have you know at  least a set of epics probably some  master works to go in there again  depending on skill level and a bunch of  things but but for those kind of high  end players we want this almost infinite  chase right that you can keep pushing  harder difficulties for kind of bragging  rights amongst your friends to try and  get that better gear and then over time  we'll see how that goes and we might add  more difficulties beyond that it sounds  like difficulty will be a significant  part of anthems endgame but Irving also  shed some light on legendary contracts  and how they plan to 